# Portfolio UX

Principle: **maximum competent UX, minimum useless UI.**

The site is a demo of production craft. Every change must read as work a Vue/Nuxt owner would ship - not a decorative landing.

Useless UI is noise that does not help the page job. Useful UI is still UI: type, color, components, states. Do not flatten the site into an unstyled document.

Human docs: `docs/design.md`, `docs/works-plan.md`. Content canon: `app/data/profile.ts`.

## Page job (top to bottom)

1. Who / role / where
2. Why hire (ownership, Vue/Nuxt, design)
3. Portfolio
4. Contact within one action

If a block does not move this path - delete it.

## Required practices

### Accessibility
- Skip link to main content
- Keyboard operable; visible `:focus-visible`
- Landmark regions; one `h1`; logical `h2+`
- Contrast that holds on paper background
- Real `alt` on work images; decorative images empty `alt`

### Typography & layout
- One column; predictable spacing scale
- Readable measure (`max-w-page` / prose width)
- Hierarchy via type and weight - not cards, shadows, gradients
- System or one self-hosted face; no font packs “for mood”

### Interaction
- Links look like links; one accent color for actions
- Hover, focus, visited, and active/tap states
- Shared press for boxed controls (`main.css`): hover slightly scales up and tints; active/tap slightly scales down. Obvious buttons keep a 2px transparent outline at rest so `outline-color` can transition; on press it becomes a darker shade of the button face (same hue). Brand tiles use a darker shade of the brand color, not a gray mix of the wash. Photos use an ink wash instead of recoloring pixels. Text links stay color + underline (do not scale glyphs).
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (no press scale)
- Tap targets usable on mobile (~44px)
- Anchors with `scroll-margin` under the header
- Prefer page + anchors + external URLs over modals

### Performance & delivery
- Prefer static (`nuxt generate`); no backend for the brochure site
- Images only for real work; sized; modern formats when added
- Work screenshots are dual-res (preview + full for lightbox). Pipeline: `.cursor/rules/work-images.mdc`, `scripts/work-images.mjs`, `docs/works-plan.md` (Assets)
- NDA without publishable shots: validated abstract diagram + pitch on the card; facts on the case page (`docs/case-diagrams.md`). Do not invent screenshots; do not treat the diagram as lightbox media
- No Lottie, marquee, grain, glow, fake stats, or motion for wow

### Content & SEO
- English UI copy aligned with CV
- Honest `title` / `description` / `lang`
- Traceable cases: name, role, stack, outcome, one real link
- No dead CTAs, invented metrics, or client IP without clearance
- No AI typography artifacts in site copy (see `.cursor/rules/content.mdc`): no em/en dashes, guillemets, decorative `<>` / arrows

### Design system signal
- Tokens: paper / ink / accent (see `tailwind.config.ts`)
- Reuse patterns; do not invent one-off chrome per section
- Dribbble shots are artifacts; site chrome stays neutral
- Stack keywords: use `TechText` so logos sit inline before names already in the sentence (not a separate tech row). Registry: `app/data/tech.ts`

## Anti-patterns

```text
BAD: Full-viewport marketing hero, glass nav, gradient CTAs
BAD: Modal case studies when a link or inline block is enough
BAD: Decorative grids, stickers, fake dashboards
BAD: Copying shot aesthetics onto the shell
```

```text
GOOD: Compact identity hero + clear sections
GOOD: List/grid of real work with one primary action each
GOOD: Quiet shell; craft shows in type, contrast, focus, speed
```

When unsure: ship clarity and standards over ornament. Do not invent a restyle unless asked.
